1
00:00:03,330 --> 00:00:05,540
Hey. You're not gonna believe this.

2
00:00:05,790 --> 00:00:08,540
I made up a joke and sent it in to Playboy.

3
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:10,710
They printed it. Yeah.

4
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:14,680
I didn't know they prints jokes.

5
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:17,680
They print jokes, interviews, hard-hitting journalism.

6
00:00:17,930 --> 00:00:19,720
It's not just about the pictures.

7
00:00:19,930 --> 00:00:22,430
It didn't work on Mom, it's not gonna work on us.

8
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:25,730
Here, check it out. It's the first one too.

9
00:00:27,190 --> 00:00:28,480
Right there.

10
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:30,860
Ha, ha.

11
00:00:31,110 --> 00:00:32,360
That is funny.

12
00:00:32,610 --> 00:00:34,700
It was also funny when I made it up.

13
00:00:36,910 --> 00:00:38,870
- What?     - I made that joke up.

14
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:40,910
Uh, oh, oh. No, you didn't. I did.

15
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:43,410
Uh, uh, oh. Yes, I did. I told Dan

16
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:45,660
and he said it was the funniest joke he'd ever heard.

17
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,920
Hey, tell Dan thanks.

18
00:00:52,380 --> 00:00:53,420
What?

19
00:00:53,670 --> 00:00:57,380
I'm sorry. I was just reading the joke below it. Man, that one is funny.

20
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:03,100
Monica, you remember me telling you that joke, right?

21
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:05,140
- No.     - Seriously?

22
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:07,440
You tell a lot of jokes.

23
00:01:09,270 --> 00:01:10,440
Look, it's my joke.

24
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,070
But if it makes you feel any better, they don't print the name.

25
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:16,780
So it doesn't really matter who gets credit.

26
00:01:16,990 --> 00:01:17,990
Yeah, I guess.

27
00:01:18,530 --> 00:01:20,910
- Hey, guys.     - Joey, Playboy printed my joke!

28
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:23,950
No, it's mine! It's my joke. Call them! They'll tell you!

29
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:25,250
- My joke!     - My joke!

30
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:26,870
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

31
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:28,960
Jokes? What...?

32
00:01:29,170 --> 00:01:31,750
You guys know they have naked chicks in there, right?

33
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:37,000

34
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:16,630
Dude! You have got to turn on Behind The Music.

35
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:20,430
The band Heart is having a really tough time and they may break up.

36
00:02:20,680 --> 00:02:22,640
Let's watch that at your place.

37
00:02:22,890 --> 00:02:26,310
Monica's watching a show. I don't want to miss when they were skinny.

38
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:29,520
Hey, Chandler. You know what we should do?

39
00:02:29,770 --> 00:02:33,400
You and I should go out and get some new sunglasses.

40
00:02:33,770 --> 00:02:36,070
What? No, I want to watch this.

41
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:42,570
- Did your cable go out?     - No. No, that's VH1.

42
00:02:42,950 --> 00:02:45,700
I gotta tell you, the music these kids listen to today...

43
00:02:45,910 --> 00:02:47,410
it's a lot of noise to me.

44
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:51,330
Why is your cable out?

45
00:02:51,540 --> 00:02:55,170
Uh... Oh, because I haven't really paid the bill. Heh, heh.

46
00:02:55,670 --> 00:02:58,880
If you need money, would you please let me loan you some money?

47
00:02:59,130 --> 00:03:01,550
No, Chandler. Forget about it, okay?

48
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:05,760
I know things have been tight since Janine moved out. God, was she hot.

49
00:03:05,970 --> 00:03:07,810
- Whoa.     - I know, yeah.

50
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:12,020
Look, I can handle it, all right? I can listen to the radio.

51
00:03:12,230 --> 00:03:15,270
And Ross gave me this great book.

52
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:19,690
Want to see if the joke stealer will let us watch the show at his place?

53
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:21,150
Sure.

54
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:25,950
- Paid your phone bill?     - Not so much.

55
00:03:32,960 --> 00:03:34,750
- Hey.     - Oh.

56
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:36,590
It's only you.

57
00:03:37,380 --> 00:03:39,960
- What are you doing?     - We are looking at a Playboy.

58
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:41,380
I want to look too!

59
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:45,970
Yikes!

60
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:50,970
Do you think these pictures are trying to tell a story?

61
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:54,230
Sure. Like in the case of this young woman...

62
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:56,730
she has lost her clothes.

63
00:03:56,980 --> 00:04:01,990
So she rides naked on the horse, she's crying out, "Where are they? Where are they?"

64
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:06,620
She's not gonna find them, lying in the grass like that.

65
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:10,990
Oh. Yeah.

66
00:04:11,250 --> 00:04:13,830
Remember the days when you'd go out to the barn...

67
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:16,710
- lift up your shirt and bend over?     - Yeah.

68
00:04:20,380 --> 00:04:23,510
You see, now, I would date this girl.

69
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:26,340
She's cute, she's outdoorsy.

70
00:04:26,590 --> 00:04:29,760
And she knows how to build a fire. That'll come in handy.

71
00:04:30,470 --> 00:04:31,520
I got a question.

72
00:04:31,850 --> 00:04:35,390
If you had to pick one of us to date, who would it be?

73
00:04:36,310 --> 00:04:37,940
- I don't know.     - Me neither.

74
00:04:38,190 --> 00:04:39,560
Rachel.

75
00:04:40,690 --> 00:04:41,730
What?

76
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:45,200
I don't know.

77
00:04:45,990 --> 00:04:47,280
Me neither.

78
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:53,950
You know, you forget how many great songs Heart had.

79
00:04:54,210 --> 00:04:55,410
Yeah.

80
00:04:56,960 --> 00:05:00,840
"Barracuda" was the first song I learned to play on the keyboard.

81
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:04,590
So you heard it, you repeated it...

82
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:07,510
so that must mean you wrote it.

83
00:05:09,550 --> 00:05:12,350
Oh, you guys with this joke. Well, I gotta say...

84
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:15,390
I know I cracked up, but I'm not even sure I got it.

85
00:05:15,810 --> 00:05:17,060
What?

86
00:05:17,770 --> 00:05:19,020
You didn't get it?

87
00:05:19,270 --> 00:05:21,520
The doctor is a monkey.

88
00:05:23,110 --> 00:05:25,650
And monkeys can't write out prescriptions.

89
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:30,870
You are not allowed to laugh at my joke.

90
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:33,160
Your joke?

91
00:05:33,370 --> 00:05:36,290
Well, I think the Hef would disagree.

92
00:05:36,540 --> 00:05:38,830
Which is why he sent me a check...

93
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:41,290
for $100.

94
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:44,840
So you stole my joke and you stole my money?

95
00:05:45,210 --> 00:05:47,130
I was gonna stick it in the ATM.

96
00:05:47,380 --> 00:05:50,260
But now I think I'll show the sexy teller...

97
00:05:50,510 --> 00:05:53,310
that I am a published writer.

98
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:55,770
Well, she'll know that you stole the joke.

99
00:05:56,020 --> 00:05:57,480
You gonna follow me down there?

100
00:05:57,730 --> 00:05:59,520
- Yeah.     - I'm not gonna go now.

101
00:05:59,770 --> 00:06:01,100
Okay.

102
00:06:03,900 --> 00:06:05,820
- Here you go.     - Oh.

103
00:06:06,190 --> 00:06:07,360
Ah.

104
00:06:07,950 --> 00:06:09,610
Uh, Gunther?

105
00:06:10,110 --> 00:06:12,620
I can't pay for this now, because I'm not working.

106
00:06:12,870 --> 00:06:15,490
I've had to cut down on some luxuries like...

107
00:06:15,700 --> 00:06:18,210
paying for stuff, so...

108
00:06:19,870 --> 00:06:21,960
Well, if you want, you can work here.

109
00:06:22,790 --> 00:06:24,040
Uh, I don't know.

110
00:06:24,250 --> 00:06:25,500
It's just...

111
00:06:26,010 --> 00:06:29,260
See, I was a regular on a soap opera, you know?

112
00:06:29,470 --> 00:06:32,390
And to go from that to this, it's just...

113
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:35,430
And plus, I'd have to wait on all my friends.

114
00:06:35,810 --> 00:06:37,430
Okay. But the money's good.

115
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:40,520
Plus, you get to stare at Rachel as much as you want.

116
00:06:43,190 --> 00:06:44,480
What?

117
00:06:44,690 --> 00:06:46,780
Flexible hours.

118
00:06:48,030 --> 00:06:49,820
Maybe I could be a waiter.

119
00:06:50,070 --> 00:06:51,450
Could I use the phone?

120
00:06:58,750 --> 00:07:00,040
She picked Rachel.

121
00:07:00,290 --> 00:07:04,710
She tried to back out of it, but it was obvious. She picked Rachel.

122
00:07:05,210 --> 00:07:08,050
He took my joke. He just took it.

123
00:07:08,880 --> 00:07:11,510
This is wrong. You know what else is wrong?

124
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:13,470
Phoebe picking Rachel.

125
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:15,600
You know who else picked Rachel? Ross.

126
00:07:15,850 --> 00:07:18,680
You know what else Ross did? He stole my joke.

127
00:07:20,350 --> 00:07:22,690
I'm gonna get a joke journal, you know?

128
00:07:22,940 --> 00:07:26,400
And document the date and time of every single one of my jokes.

129
00:07:26,610 --> 00:07:28,900
Good idea. Know what's a bad idea?

130
00:07:29,150 --> 00:07:31,400
- Picking Rachel.     - That's right.

131
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:35,620
Did you hear something?

132
00:07:35,870 --> 00:07:40,000
Maybe it's the sound of Ross climbing into my brain and stealing my thoughts.

133
00:07:40,660 --> 00:07:42,870
It's coming from the living room.

134
00:07:49,130 --> 00:07:50,380
I finished my book.

135
00:07:58,140 --> 00:08:00,600
- Hey, you guys.     - Hey.

136
00:08:00,850 --> 00:08:02,890
Don't you guys look cute.

137
00:08:03,350 --> 00:08:05,060
You guys make a cute couple.

138
00:08:06,730 --> 00:08:08,190
Monica, what are you doing?

139
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:12,490
Just trying to re-create some of the fun that we had at my place the other day.

140
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:15,030
Remember? When you picked Rachel over me?

141
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:17,780
That was funny. Ha, ha, ha.

142
00:08:17,990 --> 00:08:20,620
- It was kind of funny.     - It wasn't funny at all!

143
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:23,790
Why would you do that?

144
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:25,960
Why didn't you pick me?

145
00:08:26,210 --> 00:08:27,500
Fine.

146
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:31,880
The reason I was leaning a little bit more toward Rachel than you...

147
00:08:32,090 --> 00:08:33,970
is just, you know, you're...

148
00:08:34,630 --> 00:08:36,720
high maintenance. Let's go to lunch.

149
00:08:36,970 --> 00:08:39,390
That is completely untrue.

150
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:41,930
You think I'm high maintenance? Prove it.

151
00:08:42,180 --> 00:08:45,770
You write out a list, and we'll go through it point by point.

152
00:08:47,980 --> 00:08:50,070
No, you're right, you're easygoing.

153
00:08:51,940 --> 00:08:55,570
You're just not as easygoing as Rachel. She's just more...

154
00:08:55,820 --> 00:08:58,110
flexible and mellow. That's all.

155
00:09:01,540 --> 00:09:03,750
Well, people are different.

156
00:09:04,830 --> 00:09:08,880
Yeah, Rachel will do whatever you want. You can just walk all over her.

157
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:13,920
What? Are you saying, that I'm a pushover? I'm not a pushover.

158
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:17,340
Oh, okay. You're not a pushover.

159
00:09:18,890 --> 00:09:21,760
You think I'm a pushover. Well, watch this.

160
00:09:22,010 --> 00:09:23,850
You're not invited to lunch!

161
00:09:24,100 --> 00:09:26,560
What do you think? I think that's pretty strong.

162
00:09:26,810 --> 00:09:29,020
Come on, Monica, let's go to lunch.

163
00:09:31,270 --> 00:09:33,780
You start working on that list.

164
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:38,860
- I cannot believe her.     - I know. Where do you want to eat?

165
00:09:39,070 --> 00:09:40,950
Oh... Oh, I love that Japanese place.

166
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:43,620
I'm sick of Japanese. Not going there.

167
00:09:43,870 --> 00:09:46,330
- Wherever you want to go is cool.     - All right.

168
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:50,960

169
00:09:51,380 --> 00:09:52,630
Oh, hey, Gunther...

170
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:54,460
check this out.

171
00:09:57,170 --> 00:09:59,680
Yeah. Man, that Chandler cracks me up.

172
00:10:03,850 --> 00:10:06,810
Hey, Ross, you want anything to drink? I'm heading up there.

173
00:10:07,230 --> 00:10:09,440
- Yeah. I'll take a coffee. Thanks.     - Sure.

174
00:10:10,020 --> 00:10:11,270
- Coffee?     - No.

175
00:10:11,520 --> 00:10:13,060
Coffee? I'm going up there.

176
00:10:13,270 --> 00:10:14,520
- No.     - No, thank you.

177
00:10:16,030 --> 00:10:18,490
You need anything? I'm heading up there.

178
00:10:18,950 --> 00:10:20,240
I'd love ice water.

179
00:10:20,490 --> 00:10:21,990
You got it.

180
00:10:23,370 --> 00:10:24,700
Joey, what are you doing?

181
00:10:24,950 --> 00:10:26,290
Just being friendly.

182
00:10:28,540 --> 00:10:31,040
Joey, you're not supposed to go back there.

183
00:10:31,290 --> 00:10:33,250
No, it's okay. Right, Gunther?

184
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:36,170
Don't wink at me.

185
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:39,300
And put on your apron.

186
00:10:41,260 --> 00:10:42,510
Okay. Heh, heh.

187
00:10:42,760 --> 00:10:46,390
I don't see you asking other paying customers to put on aprons.

188
00:10:47,730 --> 00:10:50,440
- Joey, do you work here?     - No.

189
00:10:50,690 --> 00:10:52,190
- Waiter.     - Yeah!

190
00:10:58,780 --> 00:11:01,660
Joey, what's going on? Why didn't you tell us you work here?

191
00:11:01,860 --> 00:11:03,070
Uh...

192
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:09,370
It's kind of embarrassing. I mean, I was an actor, now I'm a waiter.

193
00:11:09,620 --> 00:11:11,830
It's supposed to go in the other direction.

194
00:11:12,670 --> 00:11:15,380
So's your apron. You're wearing it like a cape.

195
00:11:16,710 --> 00:11:19,800
I mean, the job's easy and the money's good, you know?

196
00:11:20,050 --> 00:11:23,970
I guess if I'm hanging out here, I might as well get paid for it. Right?

197
00:11:24,220 --> 00:11:27,430
I just feel kind of weird serving you guys, you know?

198
00:11:27,640 --> 00:11:28,770
It'll be great.

199
00:11:29,020 --> 00:11:31,430
Come on, I did it and it was fine.

200
00:11:31,640 --> 00:11:33,140
Why would it be weird?

201
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:36,360
Hey, Joey? Can I get some coffee?

202
00:11:37,530 --> 00:11:39,570
Okay. It doesn't seem that weird.

203
00:11:39,820 --> 00:11:42,490
Seriously, I asked before. You still haven't gotten it.

204
00:11:44,240 --> 00:11:46,450
See, now it's weird again.

205
00:11:47,160 --> 00:11:50,580
I think it's great. You're gonna make a lot of money. Here's your first tip.

206
00:11:51,960 --> 00:11:55,000
Don't eat yellow snow. Ha, ha, ha.

207
00:11:56,670 --> 00:11:59,300
2: 15, coffeehouse.

208
00:12:01,260 --> 00:12:04,380
This is great. Finally, I have someone I can pass my wisdom to.

209
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:07,550
Let me tell you some things I learned working at the coffeehouse.

210
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:10,850
First, the customer is always right.

211
00:12:12,060 --> 00:12:14,560
A smile goes a long way.

212
00:12:16,310 --> 00:12:19,980
And if anyone is ever rude to you, sneeze muffin.

213
00:12:21,940 --> 00:12:22,990
Thanks, Rach.

214
00:12:24,820 --> 00:12:27,740
Hey, look, you guys are just terrific, you know?

215
00:12:27,990 --> 00:12:31,080
How about clearing out so I can get some new customers, huh?

216
00:12:31,290 --> 00:12:33,370
It's all about turnover.

217
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:36,370
Joey.

218
00:12:36,580 --> 00:12:38,540
Seriously, can I get my coffee?

219
00:12:40,050 --> 00:12:42,130
I'm sorry, Ross. I'll get it right now.

220
00:12:42,630 --> 00:12:45,470
And since you wait, I'll toss in a free muffin.

221
00:12:51,890 --> 00:12:53,890
Phoebe, we'd like to talk to you.

222
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:55,690
Okay.

223
00:12:55,980 --> 00:12:59,060
So, maybe I am a little high maintenance.

224
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:02,190
And maybe Rachel is a little bit of a pushover.

225
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:04,110
But you know what we decided you are?

226
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:08,070
We are sorry to tell you this, but you, Phoebe, are flaky.

227
00:13:08,280 --> 00:13:09,450
Ha!

228
00:13:11,540 --> 00:13:13,330
That's true, I am flaky.

229
00:13:14,830 --> 00:13:18,420
So, what, you're just okay with being flaky?

230
00:13:18,670 --> 00:13:20,290
Yeah, totally.

231
00:13:21,170 --> 00:13:23,670
Then I'm okay with being high maintenance.

232
00:13:23,920 --> 00:13:26,800
Yeah. And I am okay with being a pushover.

233
00:13:27,220 --> 00:13:29,390
That's great. Good for you guys.

234
00:13:30,050 --> 00:13:32,810
- I am not high maintenance!     - I am not a pushover!

235
00:13:34,350 --> 00:13:36,560
- Who said you were?     - You did!

236
00:13:36,770 --> 00:13:39,150
I'm flaky. I'll say anything.

237
00:13:45,360 --> 00:13:46,610
Hey, Gunther.

238
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:49,240
Can you cover for me? I got an audition.

239
00:13:49,570 --> 00:13:51,990
No, I'm leaving to get my hair dyed.

240
00:13:53,870 --> 00:13:55,700
Really? I like your natural color.

241
00:13:58,290 --> 00:14:01,710
It's a great part. Check it out. I'm the lead guy's best friend.

242
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:04,300
I wait for him in this bar and save his seat. Listen.

243
00:14:05,300 --> 00:14:07,630
"I'm sorry, that seat's saved."

244
00:14:09,800 --> 00:14:13,850
- That's the whole part?     - Okay, maybe he's not his best friend, but...

245
00:14:14,220 --> 00:14:16,350
Okay, I'll see you in an hour.

246
00:14:16,680 --> 00:14:18,270
Oh, man.

247
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:22,270
I could totally get that part. "I'm sorry, this seat is taken."

248
00:14:22,520 --> 00:14:25,820
- Excuse me.     - No, I didn't mean you.

249
00:14:26,070 --> 00:14:27,320
But you believed me, huh?

250
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:31,410
I believed you were saving this seat for someone.

251
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:33,740
So you'd hire me, right?

252
00:14:34,830 --> 00:14:36,620
For what?

253
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:39,870
Exactly! All right, everybody listen up!

254
00:14:40,120 --> 00:14:42,880
The coffeehouse will be closed for about an hour.

255
00:14:43,130 --> 00:14:45,250
What?

256
00:14:45,710 --> 00:14:47,090
It's for the kids.

257
00:14:47,340 --> 00:14:50,090
Yeah, to keep the kids off drugs.

258
00:14:50,340 --> 00:14:53,930
Yeah. It's a very important issue in this month's Playboy.

259
00:14:54,140 --> 00:14:56,010
I'm sure you all read about it.

260
00:15:06,530 --> 00:15:08,740
- It's my joke.     - It's my joke.

261
00:15:11,950 --> 00:15:13,780
It's my joke.

262
00:15:15,280 --> 00:15:17,620
I don't think we're gonna settle this.

263
00:15:17,830 --> 00:15:20,500
- No. Let's have Monica decide.     - Yeah.

264
00:15:21,210 --> 00:15:22,790
- Hey, Mon!     - Mon, get out here!

265
00:15:23,040 --> 00:15:25,000
- Monica?     - Okay.

266
00:15:25,210 --> 00:15:27,550
You have to help us decide whose joke this is.

267
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:28,800
Why do I have to?

268
00:15:29,050 --> 00:15:31,170
- You're the only one that can be fair.     - Yeah.

269
00:15:31,430 --> 00:15:33,300
I can't be. You're my boyfriend.

270
00:15:33,510 --> 00:15:35,640
But I'm your brother. We're family.

271
00:15:35,850 --> 00:15:39,680
That's the most important thing in the world.

272
00:15:41,690 --> 00:15:43,440
Don't try to sway her.

273
00:15:43,810 --> 00:15:46,690
I'm your only chance to have a baby.

274
00:15:50,530 --> 00:15:52,030
- Okay, let's go.     - All right.

275
00:15:52,280 --> 00:15:55,870
We'll each tell you how we came up with the joke...

276
00:15:56,120 --> 00:16:00,080
then you decide which one of us is telling the truth. Me.

277
00:16:00,790 --> 00:16:02,040
Chandler, you go first.

278
00:16:02,290 --> 00:16:05,670
I thought of the joke two months ago at lunch with Steve.

279
00:16:05,920 --> 00:16:08,420
- Did I meet him at Christmas?     - Can I finish my story?

280
00:16:08,670 --> 00:16:10,130
Do you want me to pick you?

281
00:16:11,380 --> 00:16:14,630
See, I would never snap at you like that.

282
00:16:16,510 --> 00:16:19,060
Two babies.

283
00:16:22,980 --> 00:16:24,230
- Continue.     - Okay.

284
00:16:24,440 --> 00:16:29,150
Steve said he had to go to the doctor. And his doctor's name is Dr. Mompey.

285
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:34,450
I said, "Dr. Monkey?" And that is how the whole Dr. Monkey thing came up.

286
00:16:38,780 --> 00:16:40,410
Are you kidding?

287
00:16:41,120 --> 00:16:43,540
Okay, look, I study evolution.

288
00:16:43,790 --> 00:16:45,210
Remember? Evolution.

289
00:16:45,460 --> 00:16:47,000
Monkey into man.

290
00:16:47,250 --> 00:16:48,920
Plus, I'm a doctor. And...

291
00:16:49,170 --> 00:16:52,170
I had a monkey.

292
00:16:54,340 --> 00:16:56,260
I'm Dr. Monkey!

293
00:16:59,010 --> 00:17:01,350
- I'm not arguing with that.     - All right.

294
00:17:01,680 --> 00:17:03,730
I've heard enough. I've made my decision.

295
00:17:03,980 --> 00:17:05,560
- Oh!     - Okay, so what...? Do tell.

296
00:17:05,810 --> 00:17:07,980
You are both idiots.

297
00:17:09,650 --> 00:17:12,230
The joke is not funny, and it's offensive to women.

298
00:17:12,480 --> 00:17:14,610
And doctors. And monkeys.

299
00:17:16,030 --> 00:17:18,160
You shouldn't argue over who gets credit.

300
00:17:18,410 --> 00:17:23,240
You should be arguing over who gets blamed for inflicting this horrible joke upon the world.

301
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:24,910
Now, let it go.

302
00:17:25,120 --> 00:17:27,000
The joke sucks.

303
00:17:32,880 --> 00:17:34,760
- It's your joke.     - It is not.

304
00:17:50,190 --> 00:17:53,690
- Oh, my God, Chandler, there you are.     - Hi.

305
00:17:54,400 --> 00:17:56,440
Hey, it's Phoebe and Rachel.

306
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:58,070
Why don't you tell them...

307
00:17:58,280 --> 00:18:01,820
what you were telling me earlier about me not being high maintenance.

308
00:18:04,620 --> 00:18:08,500
Monica is a self-sufficient, together lady.

309
00:18:10,330 --> 00:18:13,250
Being with her has been like being on a vacation.

310
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:18,550
And what may be perceived as high maintenance...

311
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:21,430
is merely attention to detail...

312
00:18:21,640 --> 00:18:22,970
and...

313
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:26,430
generosity of spirit.

314
00:18:28,270 --> 00:18:33,020
Wow. You know what? That is the best fake speech I think I've ever heard.

315
00:18:33,270 --> 00:18:34,980
Really? I've heard better.

316
00:18:36,030 --> 00:18:39,110
Wait, he came up with that himself. Tell them, Chandler.

317
00:18:40,410 --> 00:18:42,410
I'm out of words. Should I say it again?

318
00:18:42,660 --> 00:18:44,620
Look, I am not high maintenance!

319
00:18:44,870 --> 00:18:46,700
I am not. Chandler!

320
00:18:49,410 --> 00:18:50,750
You're high maintenance.

321
00:18:52,170 --> 00:18:53,880
You are on my list!

322
00:18:55,420 --> 00:18:57,420
Look, I'm sorry, but you're not...

323
00:18:57,670 --> 00:19:00,470
You're not easygoing, but you're passionate.

324
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:01,970
And that's good.

325
00:19:02,220 --> 00:19:06,100
And when you get upset about little things, I think I'm pretty good...

326
00:19:06,350 --> 00:19:08,180
at making you feel better about that.

327
00:19:08,430 --> 00:19:11,350
That's good too. They say you're high maintenance...

328
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:14,190
but it's okay, because I like...

329
00:19:15,940 --> 00:19:17,940
maintaining you.

330
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:28,580
I didn't even tell him to say that.

331
00:19:29,580 --> 00:19:30,960
- Aw.     - Okay.

332
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:34,630
- All right, you're off my list.     - I'm off the list.

333
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,290
Phoebe?

334
00:19:37,500 --> 00:19:40,670
It's okay that you don't want me to be your girlfriend.

335
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:42,630
Because I have the best boyfriend.

336
00:19:44,180 --> 00:19:47,560
You know, suddenly I find you very attractive.

337
00:19:50,770 --> 00:19:52,270
How'd the audition go?

338
00:19:52,520 --> 00:19:53,900
Oh, not good. No.

339
00:19:54,100 --> 00:19:57,820
I didn't get the part. And I lost my job here, so...

340
00:19:58,070 --> 00:19:59,940
Wow, that is a bad audition.

341
00:20:02,110 --> 00:20:04,660
Well, how did you lose your job here?

342
00:20:04,910 --> 00:20:06,160
I had the audition...

343
00:20:06,410 --> 00:20:10,040
but Gunther said I had to stay so he could get his hair dyed.

344
00:20:10,250 --> 00:20:12,410
So I went anyway, and he fired me.

345
00:20:12,660 --> 00:20:15,500
He left work in the middle of the day to do a personal errand...

346
00:20:15,710 --> 00:20:19,090
and left you in charge when you've been here two days?

347
00:20:19,340 --> 00:20:20,630
That's not right.

348
00:20:21,130 --> 00:20:23,010
What are you gonna do?

349
00:20:23,220 --> 00:20:25,930
Joey, you can't let him get away with that.

350
00:20:26,140 --> 00:20:29,310
I won't let him get away with that. I'm gonna say something to him...

351
00:20:29,560 --> 00:20:32,850
I really shouldn't say anything. No, I should say something to him!

352
00:20:36,150 --> 00:20:39,270
Gunther? I want you to give Joey his job back.

353
00:20:39,520 --> 00:20:43,690
- That is really not fair that you have to fire him...     - Okay.

354
00:20:46,870 --> 00:20:49,370
- What?     - He can have his job back.

355
00:20:50,830 --> 00:20:53,830
That's right, he can have his job back.

356
00:20:55,420 --> 00:20:57,830
Glad we got that all straightened out.

357
00:20:59,130 --> 00:21:00,460
There you go, Joey.

358
00:21:00,710 --> 00:21:04,130
- Got your job back.     - That's great. Thanks, Rach.

359
00:21:04,380 --> 00:21:07,220
Pretty nice, huh? Now who's a pushover?

360
00:21:07,930 --> 00:21:10,140
- Rach, you're in my seat.     - I'm sorry.

361
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:19,480
Hey, I never got to hear who you'd pick to be your girlfriend.

362
00:21:19,820 --> 00:21:23,110
- I'd pick you, Phoebe.     - Yeah, definitely you, Pheebs.

363
00:21:23,360 --> 00:21:24,900
Yeah, I kind of thought.

364
00:21:28,660 --> 00:21:31,280
- Never.     - It would totally be you.

365
00:21:32,240 --> 00:21:33,330
Hey.

366
00:21:33,540 --> 00:21:36,870
A question: If you had to pick one of the other two to go out with...

367
00:21:37,120 --> 00:21:38,580
who would you pick?

368
00:21:38,880 --> 00:21:40,210
- No way.     - I'm not answering.

369
00:21:40,460 --> 00:21:41,960
Joey.

370
00:21:44,920 --> 00:21:47,470
No way, I'm not answering that.

